## Forensics

For an explicit wave, bootstrap-Merger first creates the manifest and hypotheses and
`BOOTSTRAP_WAVE_SPEC`, then the parallel fan-out runs with LOGS+CODE+DOCS (DATA
only for DB/API) and bounded `BLUEPRINT-SCOUT` slots with the selected `CATALOG_ID`,
when a local reference registry is available;
groups are not sequential stages. After the join, post-wave Merger saves separate
slot reports, runs the Root-depth gate, and
returns a `ControllerAction`. Candidate actions after Advocate settlement are
`NEXT_WAVE_SPEC`, `END`, or `HARD_BLOCKER`. Every
post-wave Proposal uses the Advocate gate once per `proposal_id`:
`AdvocatePacket` `CLEAN`|`HOLE`; material HOLE is not accepted;
`HARD_BLOCKER` gets at most one `BLOCKER_RECOVERY` (forbidden at wave 20).
Boss checkpoints accepted NEXT at wave 10 and wave 20. Later
waves close only recorded gaps and use the same parallel
fan-out. Reference coverage uses only Merger-qualified `zone ×
reference entry` pairs after relevance/applicability/causal/impact gates;
the full catalog Cartesian product is forbidden by default. For ordinary edits, use targeted
Read/search and edit; see
`normal-agent-workflow.mdc`. Tenets, CodeGraph/Octocode, logs, docs, and data
are evidence-driven, not a fixed sequence.

Confidence in every source/slot/Merger/root artifact is mandatory as a percentage
`0%`–`100%` with `CONFIDENCE_BASIS`; qualitative labels, decimal fractions, and
`NOT_STATED` are forbidden.

Explicit loop/wave completion is **Chat summary ALWAYS** from `rkx-loop-core`: 5 parts in
one English answer (business/UI **quoting `success_criteria`**, five-column table,
technical facts, ASCII, ✅/❌ Verdict that also quotes `success_criteria` and
`goal_closure`). Accepted `END` requires `product_goal_met` (or disclosed
`title_only_scope`). Part 5 must contain an arbitrary-length causal chain,
translation of facts into UI/business logic, and `**Basis:** *...*` /
`**Where:** *evidence-id · exact % · factual model*` according to the binding template
`rkx-loop-core`; role binding must not be presented as actual execution.
Run artifacts do not replace the chat. Mid-wave: ≤1 status line or silence;
fake summary is forbidden.

## Slack notify (phone)

Cursor Slack Cloud Agents ≠ a local Agent Chat notification. The local stop-hook
reads the exact matching `loops/<run>/deliveries/<event_id>/lifecycle.json` and sends
one of two card types: `attention` when a USER response/decision is needed or
`result` when the loop is complete. The card contains a detailed `problem_title`,
user-facing `summary`, optional `blocker`, one `next_action`,
`run · wave`.
`state/current.yaml` is not the source of user-facing verdict text. MCP sends the full
five-part verdict separately only after
`chat_itog_delivered`; the hook and MCP do not duplicate the same message class.
No artifact/conversation match — fail-open and stay silent. Secrets belong only in
`~/.cursor/rkx-slack-notify.env`.

## Browser

Built-in **cursor-ide-browser** / @Browser only (Browser Tab). Fast Vite / clean prod.
Credentials — living plan SoT, **not** in `loops/<run>/`.

**Forbidden** for post-change UI evidence: external browsers (Chrome/Safari/`xdg-open`/`open`),
“Open in Browser”, Playwright/Chrome DevTools MCP instead of Browser Tab,
`onAutoForward: "openBrowser"` on dev ports.

Remote SSH: the host listens on `127.0.0.1:5173` (+ WA `5174–5176`); the client Browser Tab uses
the forwarded Local Address from View → Ports / `.dev/forwarded-ports.env`
(`bash scripts/resolve-dev-browser-url.sh`). Procedure: skill `browser-ui-evidence`.

